  era: "Section 8 \xB7 Post-Mauryan India \xB7 c. 200 BCE \u2013 300 CE"
  title: Indo-Greeks
  text: Greek rulers from Bactria entered north-west India in the 2nd century BCE. The most famous, Menander, or Milinda, discussed philosophy with the monk Nagasena in the Milindapanha. The Indo-Greeks issued fine coins bearing their kings' portraits and names.
